<!--
This file is an executable description of how to make the S1000D data for <content>/<wiringData>/<wireGroup><wire> etc from a 
simple generic representation of data on a Mentor IXLogicDiagram.
The header area is populated by another map see ('wireHeaderMap.xml')
For this map we create the target completely – we don't merge. 

Use <isCleaningFiles val='n'/> to see the source data files for the map. The source 
of the data will be visible and will be like DiagramLogicDatax.xml
The correct technique for modifying this map is to make small incremental alterations and to rerun Publisher. 
This map will be picked up and rerun without any need to start Publisher again. 

-->
<maps>
    <!-- for  each 'XLogicDesign' in the source make a  content/wiringData-->
    <map independent='true'>
        <target>
            <path val= 'content'/>
            <path val= 'wiringData'/>
        </target>
        <source>
            <path val='XLogicDiagram'/>
        </source>
        <call target='figure' source ='$self'/>
        <call target='wireGroup' source ='$self'/>
        <call target='electricalEquipGroup' source ='$self'/>
    </map>
    <!-- for  the single 'XLogicDesign' in the source make a  wireGroup   -->
    <map target  = 'wireGroup' source  = 'XLogicDesign'>
        <call target='wireGroup' source ='XLogicDiagram'/>
    </map>
    <!-- for  each 'XLogicDiagram' in the populate the wireGroup - using 'merge' means it does not create a node, 
	which is not exactly how merge was expected to work, but 'fixing' merge now, given that merge is used in the header map
	would be unwise.  If merge was a true merge one could write this map in one stage-->
    <map target  = 'wireGroup' source  = 'XLogicDiagram' mode='merge'>
        <call target='wireGroup' source ='XLogicDiagramConductor'/>
    </map>
    <!-- for  each 'XLogicDiagramPinList' in the source make a  wire  record-->
    <map target  = 'wireGroup' source  = 'XLogicDiagramConductor' mode='merge'>
        <varif op='set' name='isDupW' source ='@dupX'/>
        <varif op='NOT_EQUAL' name='isDupW' constant='y'>
            <call target='wire' source ='$self'/>
        </varif>
    </map>
    <!-- create the single electricalEquipGroup from single XLogicDesign  -->
    <map target  = 'electricalEquipGroup' source  = 'XLogicDesign'>
        <call target='electricalEquipGroup' source ='XLogicDiagram'/>
    </map>
    <!-- for  each 'XLogicDiagram' populate the  electricalEquipGroup  -->
    <map target  = 'electricalEquipGroup' source  = 'XLogicDiagram' mode='merge'>
        <call target='electricalEquip' source ='XLogicDiagramPinList'/>
    </map>
    <!-- for  each 'XLogicDiagramPinList' in the source make a  electricalEquip  record-->
    <map target  = 'electricalEquipGroup' source  = 'XLogicDiagramPinList' mode='merge'>
        <varif op='set' name='isDup' source ='@dupX'/>
        <varif op='NOT_EQUAL' name='isDup' constant='y'>
            <call target='electricalEquip' source ='$self'/>
        </varif>
    </map>
    <map target='electricalEquip' source  = 'XLogicDiagramPinList'>
        <copy source= '@name'>
            <target>
                <path val= 'functionalItemRef'/>
                <path val= '@functionalItemNumber'/>
            </target>
        </copy>
        <copy target="partNumber" skipblank='Y'>
            <source>
                <path val= 'Attrs'/>
                <!--As in Select attr.value where name ='PartNumber'-->
                <path val= 'getAttr' param='PartNumber'/>
                <path val= '@val'/>
            </source>
        </copy>
        <!-- only add some alt if there is some to add - first we set -->
        <!-- a local var 'hasSomeAlternativeId' to the value of the id-->
        <varif op='set' name='hasSomeAlternativeId'>
            <source>
                <path val= 'Attrs'/>
                <path val= 'getAttr' param='SupplierPartNumber'/>
                <path val= '@val'/>
            </source>
        </varif>
        <!-- now execute it only if 'hasSomeAlternativeId' is not equal <> to blank-->
        <varif op='NOT_EQUAL' name='hasSomeAlternativeId' constant=''>
            <call target ='altIdentGroup' source ='$self'/>
        </varif>
        <!-- only set connectionListClass if there a value for it. First we set -->
        <!-- a local var 'hasconnectionListClass' then test it and run code conditional on that test-->
        <varif op='set' name='hasConnectionListClass'>
            <source>
                <path val= 'Props'/>
                <path val= 'getProp' param='S1000D.CLC'/>
                <path val= '@val'/>
            </source>
        </varif>
        <varif op='NOT_EQUAL' name='hasConnectionListClass' constant=''>
            <copy target="connectionListClass">
                <source>
                    <path val= 'Props'/>
                    <path val= 'getProp' param='S1000D.CLC'/>
                    <path val= '@val'/>
                </source>
            </copy>
        </varif>
        <call target='responsiblePartnerCompany' source ='$self'/>
        <!--above equipName 22.08.2014-->
        <copy target="equipName">
            <source>
                <path val= 'Attrs'/>
                <!--As in Select attr.value where name ='PartNumber'-->
                <path val= 'getAttr' param='Name'/>
                <path val= '@val'/>
            </source>
        </copy>
        <call target='reqQuantity' source ='$self'/>
        <call target='installationInfo' source ='mate'>
		    <relationship val='Mates'/>
            <relationship val='mate'/>
		</call>
    </map>
	
    <map target='installationInfo' source  = 'mate'>
        <copy target='installationLocation' skipblank='Y'> 
            <source>
                <path val= 'getParentMates'/>
                <path val= 'getParentXLogicDiagramPinList'/>
                <path val= 'Props'/>
                <path val= 'getProp' param='ZONE'/>
                <path val= '@val'/>
            </source>
        </copy>
        <copy source= '@val'>
            <target>
                <path val= 'siblingPlugIdent'/>
                <path val= 'functionalItemRef'/>
                <path val= '@functionalItemNumber'/>
            </target>
        </copy>
    </map>
    <map target='reqQuantity' source  = 'XLogicDiagramPinList'>
        <copy target= "@unitOfMeasure" constant ="EA"/>
        <copy target= "$Content" constant ="1"/>
    </map>
    <map target  = 'altIdentGroup' source  = 'XLogicDiagramPinList'>
        <call target= 'altIdent' source ='$self'/>
    </map>
    <map target  = 'altIdent' source  = 'XLogicDiagramPinList'>
        <copy target="partNumber">
            <source>
                <path val= 'Attrs'/>
                <path val= 'getAttr' param='SupplierPartNumber'/>
                <path val= '@val'/>
            </source>
        </copy>
        <copy target="manufacturerCode">
            <source>
                <path val= 'Props'/>
                <path val= 'getProp' param='S1000D.NCAGE'/>
                <path val= '@val'/>
            </source>
        </copy>
    </map>
    <!-- for  each 'XLogicDiagramPinList' in the source make a  responsiblePartnerCompany  record-->
    <map target  = 'responsiblePartnerCompany' source  = 'XLogicDiagramPinList'>
        <copy target= '@enterpriseCode'>
            <source>
                <function name='getValueFromConfigHdr'>
                    <param constant="WIRE"/>
                    <param constant="*.dmStatus.responsiblePartnerCompany.@enterpriseCode"/>
                </function>
            </source>
        </copy>
        <!-- The first param 'WIRE' simply fetches date arelated to wiring back -->
        <copy target="enterpriseName">
            <source>
                <function name='getValueFromConfigHdr'>
                    <param constant="WIRE"/>
                    <param constant="*.dmStatus.responsiblePartnerCompany.enterpriseName"/>
                </function>
            </source>
        </copy>
    </map>
    <!-- for  each 'XLogicDiagram' in the source make a single figure-->
    <map target  = 'figure' source  = 'XLogicDesign'>
        <copy target ='@xmlns' constant = 'http://www.customer.com/XSD/customerApplication'/>
    <!--    <copy target ='title' source = "@description" skipblank='N'/>  --> 
        <copy target ='title' source = "@description" skipblank='N'/>   
        <!-- Was 'description' -->
        <!--copy target ='title' constant = 'Title'/-->
        <!--   <call target='graphic' source ='$self'/>  -->
        <call target='graphic' source ='XLogicDiagram'/>
        <!--Altered this to take it from diagram-->
    </map>
    <map target  = 'figure' source  = 'XLogicDiagram'>
        <copy target ='@xmlns' constant = 'http://www.customer.com/XSD/customerApplication'/>
        <copy target ='title' source = "@description" skipblank='N'/>
        <call target='graphic' source ='$self'/>
    </map>
    <!-- create the figure/title/graphic thing and then under it create a 'hotspot' for each wire 'XLogicDiagramConductor' 
    <map target ='graphic' source  = 'XLogicDiagram'>
        <copy target ='@infoEntityIdent'>
            <source>
                <function name='getURNBody'>
                    <param>
                        <source val  ="XLogicDiagramConductor"/>
                        <source val  ="@URN"/>
                    </param>
                    <param constant="ICN"/>
                </function>
            </source>
        </copy>
        <call target='hotspot' source ='XLogicDiagramConductor'/>
    </map>
	-->
    <map target ='graphic' source  = 'XLogicDiagram'>
        <copy target ='@infoEntityIdent' source ="@icnRef"/>
        <copy target ='@reproductionHeight' constant ="130mm"/>
        <copy target ='@reproductionScale' constant ="1"/>
        <call target='hotspot' source ='XLogicDiagramConductor'/>
		<!--Added ACE 2014.09.16 call to also add pinlists-->
		 <call target='hotspot' source ='XLogicDiagramPinList'/>
    </map>
    <!--Added ACE 2014.09.16- new map for Pin list-->
    <map target  = 'hotspot' source  = 'XLogicDiagramPinList'>
        <copy target ='@applicationStructureIdent' source = "@name"/>
        <copy target ='@applicationStructureName' source = "@name"/>
        <!-- OK-->
        <copy target ='@hotspotTitle'>
            <source>
                <function name='concat'>
                    <param source="@name"/>
                    <param constant=" Device"/>
                </function>
            </source>
        </copy>
        <copy target ='@hotspotType' constant='callout'/>
    </map>
	
    <map target  = 'hotspot' source  = 'XLogicDiagramConductor' mode='nocreate'>
	     <varif op='set' name='HotSpotIdent' source ="@HotSpot"/>		    
		 <!-- note that some conductors may be invisible in which case 
	     they will have no hotspot attribute and we don't create the object. 
		 We do this by not calling the map for an object with no @HotSpot-->
		 <!-- don't execute any more map statements in this map -->
         <varif op='NOT_EQUAL' name='HotSpotIdent' constant=''>        
             <setmode mode = 'create'/>       	 
            <!--<return/> -->
         </varif>
	<!-- <setmode mode = 'create'/>  alter the mode of this map--> 		
        <copy target ='@applicationStructureIdent' source = "@HotSpot"/>
        <copy target ='@applicationStructureName' source = "@name"/>
        <!-- OK-->
        <copy target ='@hotspotTitle'>
            <source>
                <function name='concat'>
                    <param source="@name"/>
                    <param constant=" Wire Conductor"/>
                </function>
            </source>
        </copy>
        <copy target ='@hotspotType' constant='callout'/>
    </map>
    <!-- for each   'XLogicDiagramConductor' make a 'wire' and attach it to the target-->
    <map>
        <target path = 'wire'/>
        <source path ='XLogicDiagramConductor'/>
        <copy target ='@wireState' constant = 'active'/>
        <!-- set the  applicRefId from calling function  getValueFromConfigHdr('WIRE','*.referencedApplicGroup.applic.id') 
	 Gebhard Maurer 27.06.2014 - this value is not required
        <copy>
            <target path= '@applicRefId'/>
            <source>
                <function name='getValueFromConfigHdr'>
                    <param constant="WIRE"/>
                    <param constant="*.referencedApplicGroup.applic.id"/>
                </function>
            </source>
        </copy>
		-->
        <call target='wireIdent' source ='$self'/>
        <call target='wireConnection' source ='$self'/>
        <call target='wireInfo' source ='$self'/>
    </map>
    <!-- populate the wireIdent tag's wireNumber element-->
    <map>
        <target path = 'wireIdent'/>
        <source path='XLogicDiagramConductor'/>
        <copy>
            <target>
                <path val= 'wireNumber'/>
                <path val= '$Content'/>
            </target>
            <source>
                <path val = '@name'/>
            </source>
        </copy>
    </map>
    <!-- populate the wireConnection  This guy contains zero to two children-->
    <map>
        <target path = 'wireConnection'/>
        <source path='XLogicDiagramConductor'/>
        <call name='Eq' target='fromEquip' source ='XLogicDiagramPin' offset='0'/>
        <call name='Eq' target='toEquip' source ='XLogicDiagramPin' offset='1'/>
    </map>
    <!--With  'getRelatedPinList' in the following map we use a more generalised concept of a 'relationship' to make life easy.  
	 A relationship allows one to set off anywhere in the xml and find (or make) the related nodes.  Then we can continue  the  mapping from the related notes.  
     We  have informally been using the concept of a relationship before this point. The default relationship is the set of child nodes is in that relationship with its parent. -->
    <!-- populate the fromEquip or toEquip dynamically so no actual target is specified here, we call this map by name-->
    <map name='Eq' source= 'XLogicDiagramPin'>
        <copy>
            <target>
                <path val= 'functionalItemRef'/>
                <path val= '@functionalItemNumber'/>
            </target>
            <source>
                <path val='getRelatedPinList'/>
                <path val='@name'/>
            </source>
        </copy>
        <call target='contactInfo' source ='$self'/>
    </map>
    <map target = 'contactInfo' source= 'XLogicDiagramPin'>
        <call target='contact' source ='$self'/>
    </map>
    <map target = 'contact' source= 'XLogicDiagramPin'>
        <copy target = '@contactIdent' source = '@name'/>
        <copy target = '@contactPartNumber'>
            <source>
                <path val='getRelatedPinList'/>
                <path val= 'Attrs'/>
                <path val= 'getAttr' param='PartNumber'/>
                <path val= '@val'/>
            </source>
        </copy>
    </map>
    <!--
	This example is what we are trying to make - insofar as we have information to make it
	 <wireInfo>
                       
                        <harnessIdent>Lamp1</harnessIdent>
                        <wireSeqNumber>1</wireSeqNumber>
                        <circuitIdent>234</circuitIdent>
                        <sectionIdent>567</sectionIdent>
                        <twistGroup>
                            <twist twistingType="1">Lamp1</twist>
                        </twistGroup>
                        <length>1000</length>
                        <wireColor>red</wireColor>
                        <responsiblePartnerCompany enterpriseCode="U8025">
                            <enterpriseName>UK MoD</enterpriseName>
                        </responsiblePartnerCompany>
                        <routing>
                            <feedThru holeIdent="1">
                                <referenceDesignator>FT3</referenceDesignator>
                            </feedThru>
                        </routing>
                    </wireInfo>
	-->
    <map target = 'wireGauge' source ='XLogicDiagramConductor'>
        <copy target = '$Content'>
            <source>
                <path val= 'Attrs'/>
                <!--As in Select attr.value where name ='WireCSA'-->
                <path val= 'getAttr' param='WireCSA'/>
                <path val= '@val'/>
            </source>
        </copy>
        <copy>
            <target>
                <path val= '@wireGaugeType'/>
            </target>
            <source constant='proj'/>
        </copy>
    </map>
    <map target = 'wireInfo' source ='XLogicDiagramConductor'>
        <call target='wireCode' source ='$self'/>
        <copy target="partNumber" skipblank='Y'>
            <source>
                <path val= 'Attrs'/>
                <path val= 'getAttr' param='PartNumber'/>
                <path val= '@val'/>
            </source>
        </copy>
        <copy target ='harnessIdent' skipblank='Y'>
            <source>
                <path val= 'Attrs'/>
                <!--As in Select attr.value where name ='Harness'-->
                <path val= 'getAttr' param='Harness'/>
                <path val= '@val'/>
            </source>
        </copy>
        <copy target ='wireColor' skipblank='Y'>
            <source>
                <path val= 'Attrs'/>
                <path val= 'getAttr' param='WireColor'/>
                <path val= '@val'/>
            </source>
        </copy>
        <!-- now we might want make an 'illustrationRef/refs' - of the raw data has an XREF then this is required -->
        <call target='refs' source ='XREF'/>
        <!--  <call target='dmRef' source ='$self'/> -->
    </map>
    <map source ='XREF'>
        <target>
            <path val= 'illustrationRef'/>
            <path val= 'refs'/>
        </target>
        <call target='dmCode' source ='E'/>
    </map>
    <map source ='E'>
        <target>
            <path val= 'dmRef'/>
            <path val= 'dmRefIdent'/>
            <path val= 'dmCode'/>
        </target>
        <copy target='@assyCode' source = "assyCode"/>
        <!--* *-->
        <copy target='@disassyCode' source = "DC"/>
        <copy target='@disassyCodeVariant' source = "DCV"/>
        <copy target='@infoCode' source = "IC"/>
        <copy target='@infoCodeVariant' source = "ICV"/>
        <copy target='@itemLocationCode' source = "LC"/>
        <copy target='@modelIdentCode' source = "MI"/>
        <copy target='@subSubSystemCode' source = "subSubSystemCode"/>
        <!--* *-->
        <copy target='@subSystemCode' source = "subSystemCode"/>
        <!--* *-->
        <copy target='@systemCode' source = "systemCode"/>
        <!--* *-->
        <copy target='@systemDiffCode' source = "SDC"/>
    </map>
    <!--
	 <illustrationRef>
        // For references to other wiring data modules of an wire the element <illustrationRef> has to be used.
        // For each reference a element <demRef> has to be used inside of the element <refs>.
        <refs>
            <dmRef>
                <dmRefIdent>
                   <dmCode assyCode="0009" disassyCode="00" disassyCodeVariant="A" infoCode="056" infoCodeVariant="A" itemLocationCode="A" modelIdentCode="PC24" subSubSystemCode="0" subSystemCode="2" systemCode="E28" systemDiffCode="A"/>
                </dmRefIdent>
            </dmRef>
			// more here 
        </refs>
        </illustrationRef>
	
	-->
    <map target = 'wireCode' source ='XLogicDiagramConductor'>
        <copy target ='wireType'>
            <source>
                <path val= 'Attrs'/>
                <path val= 'getAttr' param='WireSpec'/>
                <path val= '@val'/>
            </source>
        </copy>
        <call target='wireGauge' source ='$self'/>
    </map>
    <!-- make xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="URN:S1000D:ICN-S1000DBIKE-AAA-D000000-0-U8025-00536-A-04-1" xlink:title="Complete bicycle" infoEntityIdent="ICN-S1000DBIKE-AAA-D000000-0-U8025-00536-A-04-1">  -->
    <!-- //////////////////// -->
    <map source ='XLogicDiagramConductor'>
        <target>
            <path val= 'illustrationRef'/>
            <path val= 'refs'/>
            <path val= 'dmRef'/>
        </target>
        <copy target ='@xlink:type' constant= 'simple'/>
        <copy target ='@xlink:href'>
            <source>
                <function name='concat'>
                    <param constant= 'URN:S1000D:'/>
                    <param>
                        <function name='getURNBody'>
                            <param source="@URN"/>
                            <param constant="ICN"/>
                        </function>
                    </param>
                </function>
            </source>
        </copy>
        <copy target ='@xlink:title' source="@name"/>
        <copy target ='@infoEntityIdent'>
            <source>
                <function name='concat'>
                    <param constant= 'URN:S1000D:'/>
                    <param>
                        <function name='getURNBody'>
                            <param source="@URN"/>
                            <param constant="ICN"/>
                        </function>
                    </param>
                </function>
            </source>
        </copy>
        <call target='OLD_hotspot' source ='$self'/>
    </map>
    <!-- //////////////////////-->
    <!-- make     <hotspot id="fig-0001-gra-0001-hot-0000" applicationStructureIdent="hot000" applicationStructureName="0" hotspotType="CALLOUT" hotspotTitle="BICYCLE" objectDescr="BICYCLE"/> -->
    <map target = 'OLD_hotspot' source ='XLogicDiagramConductor'>
        <copy target ='@id' source ='@HotSpot'/>
        <copy target ='@applicationStructureIdent' source ='@HotSpot'/>
        <copy target ='@applicationStructureName' constant= '0'/>
        <copy target ='@hotspotType' constant= 'CALLOUT'/>
        <copy target ='@hotspotTitle' source ='@name'/>
    </map>
    <!-- //////////////////////-->
    <!-- These are a relationships which are navigated on the source-->
    <!-- //////////////////////-->
    <relationship name="getRelatedPinList" side ="source">
        <origin val= 'XLogicDiagramPin'/>
        <destination val= 'XLogicDiagramPinList'/>
        <valueRule op='EQUAL'>
            <origin path='@id'/>
            <destination>
                <path val='XLogicDiagramPin'/>
                <path val='@id'/>
            </destination>
        </valueRule>
        <elementPathRule/>
    </relationship>
	<!--/////////////////////////////////////////////-->	
	<relationship name="getParentMates" side ="source">
        <origin val= 'mate'/>
        <destination val= 'Mates'/>
        <positionRule val = 'parent' offset='0'/>  
    </relationship>
	
	<relationship name="getParentXLogicDiagramPinList" side ="source">
        <origin val= 'Mates'/>
        <destination val= 'XLogicDiagramPinList'/>
        <positionRule val = 'parent' offset='0'/>  
    </relationship>
	
	
	
	
	
    <!-- /////////////////////
This is a parameterised relationship – it takes an origin parameter and compares that value with the destination path. 
Currently relationships will only interpret one parameter
    //////////////////////-->
    <relationship name="getAttr" side ="source">
        <origin val= 'Attrs'/>
        <destination val= 'A'/>
        <valueRule op='EQUAL'>
            <origin>
                <path param ='true'/>
            </origin>
            <destination path="@name"/>
        </valueRule>
        <positionRule val = 'child' offset='0'/>
        <elementPathRule/>
    </relationship>
    <!-- ///////////same type of relationship – this one gets a named property by parameter///////////-->
    <relationship name="getProp" side ="source">
        <origin val= 'Props'/>
        <destination val= 'P'/>
        <valueRule op='EQUAL'>
            <origin>
                <path param ='true'/>
            </origin>
            <destination path="@name"/>
        </valueRule>
        <positionRule val = 'child' offset='0'/>
        <elementPathRule/>
    </relationship>
    <!-- //////////////////////-->
    <!-- ////This one - (not used) shows how one can define a relationp with a constant condition//////////////////-->
    <relationship name="getPartNumber" side ="source">
        <origin val= 'Attrs'/>
        <destination val= 'A'/>
        <valueRule op='EQUAL'>
            <origin constant='PartNumber'/>
            <destination path="@name"/>
        </valueRule>
        <positionRule val = 'child' offset='0'/>
        <elementPathRule/>
    </relationship>
    <!-- //////////////////////-->
    <!-- General  Notes

The two essential concepts are
    a map which is a description of how you find/create something in one element from another element
and 
    a relationship which tells you how you navigate on one side or the other of the system 

A map usually has a source and target defined - if it doesn't then the source and target are taken from where it called.
A map may have a name.  If it has a name it can be called by name.
A map has a mode.  By default the mode is 'create'.   The modes defined are:

'create' - create (unconditional) the entire target of the map
'find'. - Find  or create - create the final target if it does not exist. Otherwise do not create but use the existing.  Identification attributes may be set. (not yet implemented)
'optional'.  - don't create the target of the map - you have to conditionally hit the keyword 'setmode' to set the mode to something else. 
'nocreate' - don't create the target of this map unless we run a create statement (we normally put the create statement in a variable )
'extant' - the target of this map already exists, just set attributes and values on it
'merge' - merge this based on identification (not yet implemented)

The target can be a path in which case it this will find or create all the elements of that path.
The mapping statements are either:
     1) 'copy' - which tells it to copy something to the target -
      2) 'call' - which tells it to call another map from the point given in the call statement.
      3) id - a set of statements identifying the final target element. 

The statement in a map run in the order they are declared.

All elements that declare a 'val' may be abbreviated ( provided we only want to declare one object with a 'val') 

Thus 

 <source>
      <path val='XLogicDesign'/>
</source>

could have been written 

 <source path ='XLogicDesign'/>

There is no difference in execution.
In the same way source and target statements may be abbrieviated 

Special attributes. 

$Content is a special attribute standing for the node content				
All attributes are  prefixed with @name.
The final target of a copy can be an element - in which case we assume the value is to be set into $Content
The source attribute $Tree makes a copy of the entire source tree below that point. 

A copy statement may take the property 'replace'   this tells it to replace the old value of an attribute or $Content with value assigned by the map. 
If no value previously existed then the new value is set in any case. 

Where a copy statment has a true path target it will make a new path for all elements to that point. 
This means that the technique is not appropriate for creating a number of attributes, single target path.  The solution to this problem is to use a call to an independent map and let that ake a single target with
potentially many properites set.

The call statement may have  up to 5 parameters
	 			
    1) name = the optional name of the transform we will call.
    2) target = the name of the item is going to be created in the transform that we call.  
          If the transform doesn't defy a target name then this will be the name of the object we create.
    3) source - the name of the source of the transform. 
    4) relationship -  the name of the relationship used to get from the current source to the source 
	      we will plug into the transform we call.  If not present it 
		  simply means we're going to use the inbuilt child relationship to that name. 	
     5) offset - the offset into the relationship navigation. If we ask from an offset which 
	     is bigger than the number of items then the transform will not be called.  If we don't
	     specify an offset at all it means it will be called for all child items.
	
For VarIf the following ops are defined:
     "SET"   - which instructs the system to set the value to named var
	 "EQUAL" , 	"NOT_EQUAL", "BIGGER",  "SMALLER", "BIGGER_OR_EQUAL","SMALLER_OR_EQUAL"
	  Thsee all instructs a system to use the value in a named varif and execute the code contained in the VarIf conditionally


Note that this document  uses pure XML attribute style.  We don't allow mixed up content nodes in this XML.

